Third-party notices
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

emgr has no C or C++ dependencies. Every image codec it uses is implemented
in Rust and statically linked into the binary:

  JPEG   jpeg-encoder, jpeg-decoder      (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND IJG
  PNG    png, via the image crate        MIT OR Apache-2.0
  GIF    gif, via the image crate        MIT OR Apache-2.0
  WebP   vaam-image-webp, a fork of      MIT OR Apache-2.0
         image-rs/image-webp
  AVIF   ravif + rav1e (encode)          BSD-2-Clause
         avif-decode + rav1d (decode)    BSD-2-Clause

The Independent JPEG Group notice above is REQUIRED and must not be removed
while jpeg-encoder is a dependency. It is easy to assume otherwise: the
notice was originally here for mozjpeg/mozjpeg-sys, which vendored IJG C
code, and the C-dependency removal replaced mozjpeg with pure Rust. But `jpeg-encoder` is itself
licensed "(MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND IJG" - its default quantisation and Huffman
tables derive from the IJG reference implementation, so reimplementing the
codec in Rust did not shed the licence. See the IJG entry in deny.toml.

rav1d is a Rust port of dav1d and carries dav1d's BSD-2-Clause licence.

Full licence texts ship with those crates and are reproduced in the
dependency tree under ~/.cargo/registry.
